// GEMMs over GGUF weights without matrix units (an M4's GPU): the prompt
// runs' projections (src/kernels/glm53.rs `gemm_with` when the device has
// no VK_KHR_cooperative_matrix) and Gemma 4 / Inkling 2 routed experts
// grouped by expert.
//
// A threadgroup of 256 computes a tile of Y (sgemm_tile.glsl), a thread 8
// activation rows x 4 weight rows: 64 x 128, or 32 x 256 for an expert's
// pairs that fit 32 rows. Small expert tiles (<= 32 pairs) keep decoded
// weights in registers and broadcast f16 activations across the subgroup
// without workgroup barriers. Inner K-steps use FP16 FMAs widened to f32
// every 32 K-elements (with f32 fallback on FP16 overflow) for 2x ALU
// throughput and ~2x FLOP/W on fanless Apple G16 GPUs.
